    <Description>&lt;span style="font-size:36px;"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:times new roman;"&gt;Operation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#2F4F4F;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:times new roman;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#B22222;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:times new roman;"&gt;Holiday Cheer!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;span style="font-size:16px;"&gt;This is a long-standing tradition for the Bellevue Chamber of Commerce &amp;amp; Community, and we are happy to keep it going this year. Operation Holiday Cheer seeks to bring a little holiday magic to our local enlisted military members that remain in the Offutt Air Force Base dorms over Christmas. Bags are filled with jolly goodies and delivered to Offutt to bring some holiday cheer.&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
Please consider making a financial or in-kind donation to enable the Bellevue Chamber of Commerce &amp;amp; Community the ability to secure items for 500 bags. All contributors are recognized on a holiday card that is included in the bag. Please make checks payable to the Bellevue Economic Enhancement Foundation (BEEF) c/o of Operation Holiday Cheer - Bellevue Chamber of Commerce &amp;amp; Community. You can also contribute via credit card through the "Register" button on the right-hand side of this screen. &lt;u&gt;Contributors of $300+ will be invited to help stuff the bags on Tuesday, December 8th &lt;em&gt;(please note that stuffing the bags is by invitation only)&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/u&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
You are also welcome to donate in-kind items! Please ensure that the items are new and that you have 500 of them so each military member receives the same items in their bag. Thank you for your generosity in helping to continue this cheerful and magical tradition for those stationed here in Bellevue!&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;u&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Donations (financial and in-kind) must be received by Tuesday, December 1st. The chamber is happy to pick up donations. Please contact us to arrange a time.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
